Training pipeline for py3langid models.

Everything runs through two commands:

1) gather_data.py - download a multi-domain corpus (tatoeba, cc100, wiki,
   leipzig; language code tables in sources.py); raw downloads are kept
   in raw_downloads/ and reused. topup.py adds generic sources (GlotCC,
   Glot500, UDHR) for thin classes via --domains topup.
     python -m py3langid.train.gather_data --output corpusN
2) train.py - single integrated trainer: index -> per-(domain,lang) n-gram
   count shards (cached) -> DF feature selection -> IG weights (lang+domain)
   -> LD feature selection -> scanner -> NB parameters -> model.npz.xz.
     python -m py3langid.train.train -m MODEL_DIR corpusN

Supporting modules (used as libraries by train.py):
  stages.py (indexing, feature selection, IG, NB parameters),
  shards.py, scanner.py, common.py

verify.py - corpus cleaning: classify training docs with a trusted model,
move mismatched docs (or strip mismatched paragraphs with --paragraphs).
  python -m py3langid.train.verify --model MODEL_FILE corpusN

The full release recipe (verify -> calibrated train -> benchmark) is driven
by benchmarks/finalize.py; see TRAINING.md.

Originally a refactoring of the langid.py training tools by Marco Lui (2013).
